# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738 slice 2: a call through a captured Structure (`loc\nope(x)`) -- the head is a path, and the
# check of a call head asks the capture what is wrong with it (l2_check_primary -> l2_cap_text): its type
# has no field `nope`.  Before, "unknown field path root".
Model:
    int: other 5
    int: value 0
end: Model

fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    loc: merge: Model
    loc\value: n
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: loc\nope(x)
    return: read

@: r40 makeReader(40)
int: a (r40: 2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
